  "body": "## What\n\nEvery native picker (Open, Model, Save, Save As, Post, machine/post/theme picks) could open\n**behind** the CamCraft window. `crates/ui/src/file_dialog.rs` built `rfd::FileDialog` with\ntitle/filters/directory only — `set_parent` was never called — and the shell never asked for\nthe foreground, so a launch from a terminal left the app (and therefore its dialogs) behind\nwhatever launched it.\n\n## The fix\n\n- `file_dialog.rs` publishes the shell window once it exists (a thread-local: winit's\n  `Window` is `!Send`, so a `OnceLock` is not an option) and hands it to rfd with\n  `set_parent`. The owner is raised just before a picker opens, so a dialog never follows a\n  background owner.\n- `shell_window.rs` publishes the window right after `create_window`, asks for the\n  foreground once at startup, and owns the GPU-refusal `MessageDialog` the same way.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Hand-checked on Windows 11, 2560×1600 at 125 %: launch the release build from a terminal,\n  first Ctrl+O — the `#32770` \"Open\" dialog is topmost in z-order and visible; the shell\n  itself is `GetForegroundWindow` after launch.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` — 531 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base main` — ok (ui suites, 26 s)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo headless test for dialog ownership: rfd modals are hand-test-only in this repo\n(`egui_app/tests.rs` says so), and a `winit::Window` cannot be created in a unit test. The\nevidence is the hand check plus the z-order probe (`EnumWindows` shows the dialog above the\nshell).\n\nChangelog: native Open/Save dialogs are owned by the shell window and no longer open behind it (#1067)\nFixes #1067\n",
